use flake

# Keep a durable GC root on the dev shell's *build-time* closure. nix-direnv
# only roots the runtime closure, so the weekly nix-gc reaps the build deps
# that a cold `nix develop` needs -- which then requires the network. This
# root lives outside .direnv so `git clean -xdf` can't take it with it.
#
# Backgrounded and nonfatal on purpose: it must never block or fail a reload
# when you're offline (there it's a no-op; everything is already rooted).
(
  nix build .#devShellInputs \
    --out-link "${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/nix/gcroots/rlox-devshell" \
    >/dev/null 2>&1 &
)
